.\" Manual page for roar(1)
.\"
.\" Hand-maintained alongside the ArgumentParser help text in
.\" Sources/Commands/*.swift. Keep the two in sync: the help text is
.\" the canonical short form (read interactively via `roar <sub> --help`);
.\" this man page is the long-form reference (read via `man roar`).
.\"
.\" To preview locally without installing:
.\"     man -l man/roar.1
.\"
.\" To install for the current user (Bash/zsh both honour MANPATH):
.\"     mkdir -p ~/.local/share/man/man1
.\"     cp man/roar.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/
.\"     export MANPATH="$HOME/.local/share/man:$MANPATH"
.\"
.\" To install system-wide (requires sudo):
.\"     sudo cp man/roar.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.\"
.TH ROAR 1 "2026-05-13" "roar 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
roar \- send macOS user notifications from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B roar
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B roar
posts notifications through Apple's
.B UserNotifications
framework so they appear in Notification Center, in the banner area, and
under Focus rules the same way any other macOS application's
notifications do. The tool ships as a small AppKit-hosted CLI: it
dispatches on a subcommand, hands off to the framework, drains the XPC
ack, and exits.
.PP
The available subcommands are
.BR send ,
.BR list ,
.BR dismiss ,
.BR clear ,
and
.BR settings .
A bare
.B roar
invocation prints the command-level help — pick a subcommand
explicitly.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS roar send [options]
Post a single notification. Most options below correspond to fields on
.IR UNMutableNotificationContent .
.TP
.BI --title " TITLE"
Notification title. Defaults to the machine's user-visible name
(System Settings \(-> General \(-> About \(-> Name), falling back to
the short hostname.
.TP
.BI --subtitle " TEXT"
Notification subtitle.
.TP
.BI "--body, -b " TEXT
Notification body. If omitted and stdin is piped, the body is read
from stdin (capped at 1 MB).
.TP
.BI --sound " NAME"
Name of a system sound to play (e.g.
.BR Glass ,
.BR Ping ),
or
.B default
for the default notification sound. The probe checks
.B /System/Library/Sounds
and
.BR /Library/Sounds .
.TP
.BI --identifier " ID"
Stable identifier. Reposting with the same identifier replaces the
prior notification in place (no flicker, no duplicate). Omit to mint
a fresh UUID per send. Max 256 characters; no NUL / control bytes.
.TP
.BI --activate-bundle-id " com.example.app"
Bundle identifier of an application to activate when the notification
is clicked.
.TP
.BI --open-url " URL"
URL to open when the notification is clicked. By default only
.BR http: ,
.BR https: ,
and
.B mailto:
are accepted; pass
.B --allow-any-url-scheme
to accept others. A built-in deny-list always rejects script-bearing
schemes (file:, javascript:, data:, applescript:, ...) even with the
override flag.
.TP
.B --allow-any-url-scheme
Allow URL schemes outside the default allow-list.
.TP
.BI --exec " CMD"
Shell command to run via
.B /bin/sh -c
when the notification is clicked. Requires
.BR --allow-shell-on-click .
.TP
.B --allow-shell-on-click
Acknowledge that
.B --exec
runs a shell command on click and proceed. Required when
.B --exec
is set.
.TP
.BI --attachment " PATH"
Local path to an image, audio file, or video to attach. Repeat for
multiple attachments (max 10). Remote URLs are rejected — pre-download
with
.B curl -o /tmp/foo
first.
.TP
.B --no-thumbnail
Suppress the small thumbnail preview macOS renders alongside the
attachment.
.TP
.BI --thumbnail-time " SECONDS"
Seconds offset into a video attachment to use for thumbnail
generation. Must be \(>= 0.
.TP
.BI --attachment-type-hint " UTI"
UTI (e.g.
.BR public.png ,
.BR public.mpeg-4 )
telling the framework how to interpret the attachment.
.TP
.BI --interruption-level " LEVEL"
Disruption tier:
.B passive
(Notification Center only),
.B active
(default, banner+NC), or
.B time-sensitive
(bypasses Focus / Do Not Disturb).
.TP
.BI --thread-id " ID"
Thread identifier for grouping related notifications in Notification
Center.
.TP
.BI --relevance-score " 0.0..1.0"
Importance hint used by macOS to rank this notification within
summaries.
.TP
.BI --in " DURATION"
Schedule firing after the given delay.
.BR <number><unit> ,
where unit is
.B s
/
.B m
/
.B h
/
.B d
(e.g.
.BR 30s ,
.BR 5m ,
.BR 1.5h ,
.BR 2d ).
Minimum 1s, maximum 365d. Mutually exclusive with
.B --at
and
.BR --repeat .
.TP
.BI --at " TIMESTAMP"
Schedule firing at a specific time. Accepted forms:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
ISO 8601 with zone:
.B 2026-12-31T17:00:00Z
or
.BR 2026-12-31T17:00:00+01:00 .
.IP \(bu 2
Local time without zone:
.B 2026-12-31T17:00:00
or
.B "2026-12-31 17:00:00"
or
.BR "2026-12-31 17:00" .
.IP \(bu 2
Date-only at local midnight:
.BR 2026-12-31 .
.RE
.IP
Past timestamps and timestamps less than 1s in the future are
rejected. Mutually exclusive with
.B --in
and
.BR --repeat .
.TP
.BI --repeat " PATTERN"
Recurring calendar schedule. Forms:
.BR hourly ,
.BR "daily:HH:MM" ,
.BR "weekly:DAY:HH:MM" ,
.BR "monthly:D:HH:MM" .
Times are interpreted in the system's current local timezone.
Mutually exclusive with
.B --in
and
.BR --at .
.TP
.BI --action " ID:TITLE[::FLAGS]"
Add a custom button. Optional
.B ::
suffix carries action flags:
.B destructive
and
.BR auth-required ,
comma-separated. Repeat for additional buttons (max 4). Requires
.BR --wait .
.TP
.BI --text-action " ID:TITLE[::FLAGS]"
Add a text-input (reply-style) action. At most one per notification.
Requires
.BR --wait .
.TP
.BI --text-placeholder " TEXT"
Placeholder shown inside the reply field for
.BR --text-action .
.TP
.BI --text-button-title " LABEL"
Label of the inline send button next to the reply field.
.TP
.BI --target-content-id " ID"
Hint string handed to the target app on click, used to route the
click to a specific window or document.
.TP
.BI --hide-previews-body-placeholder " TEXT"
Placeholder body shown when the user has set 'Show Previews' to
\&'When Unlocked' or 'Never'.
.TP
.BI --summary-format " FORMAT"
Format string for the summary line macOS renders when multiple
notifications in this category collapse together. Supports
.B %u
(unread count) and
.B %@
(comma-joined intent identifiers).
.TP
.B --show-title-when-previews-hidden
Show the notification title on the lock screen even when previews
are hidden.
.TP
.B --show-subtitle-when-previews-hidden
Show the notification subtitle on the lock screen even when
previews are hidden.
.TP
.BI --foreground-presentation " OPTION"
How the notification should appear if it arrives while
.B roar
itself is still running in the foreground (typically only the
.B --wait
flow). Repeat the flag for multiple options
.RB ( --foreground-presentation
.B banner
.B --foreground-presentation
.BR list ),
choosing from
.BR banner ,
.BR list ,
.BR sound .
.TP
.BI --filter-criteria " STRING"
Focus-filter hint handed to the framework via
.IR UNMutableNotificationContent.filterCriteria .
.TP
.B --wait
Block until the user interacts with the notification, then print
the chosen action id to stdout and exit. Exit codes:
.B 0
(default click or custom action),
.B 3
(explicit dismiss),
.B 2
(timeout from
.BR --wait-timeout ).
For a
.B --text-action
interaction, the typed text follows the action id on a second
line. Read to EOF — embedded newlines are passed through verbatim.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR --exec ,
.BR --open-url ,
and
.BR --activate-bundle-id .
.TP
.BI --wait-timeout " DURATION"
Maximum time to wait for interaction in
.B --wait
mode. Same format as
.BR --in .
Defaults to
.B 5m
so unattended scripts can't hang forever; pass a larger value
(up to 365d) to extend.
.SS roar list [--delivered | --pending] [--header]
List notifications belonging to this app. Output is tab-separated:
.BR ID ,
.BR STATUS ,
.BR TIME ,
.BR TITLE ,
.BR BODY .
Newlines and tabs in title/body are flattened to spaces.
.TP
.B --delivered
Show only delivered notifications. Mutually exclusive with
.BR --pending .
.TP
.B --pending
Show only pending (scheduled-but-not-yet-fired) notifications.
.TP
.B --header
Print a column header line before the listing.
.SS roar dismiss <id> [<id>...]
Remove the named notifications from both the delivered and pending
buckets. Unknown ids are reported on stderr; if NO id matched, the
exit code is
.B 4
(distinct from 0 = at least one matched and ArgumentParser's 64 =
usage error). At least one id matching produces exit 0 plus a stderr
warning naming the unknowns.
.SS roar clear [--delivered | --pending | --all] [--categories]
Remove notifications belonging to this app. By default, only
.B delivered
notifications are removed — pending (scheduled) requests are
preserved.
.TP
.B --delivered
Clear only delivered notifications (same as the default).
.TP
.B --pending
Clear only pending notifications.
.TP
.B --all
Clear BOTH delivered and pending. Equivalent to the historical
no-flag behaviour; opt-in now so a typo'd
.B roar clear
cannot destroy scheduled requests.
.TP
.B --categories
Prune
.B roar.dyn.*
notification categories that aren't referenced by any currently
delivered or pending notification. Safe to run any time. Combine
with a scope flag to clear and prune in one shot; pass alone to
prune without touching notifications.
.SS roar settings
Print the system's
.I UNNotificationSettings
for this bundle, one
.BI key ": " value
per line. Useful for debugging why a notification didn't play a
sound or break through Focus.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — the notification was posted (
.BR send ),
the request was queued (
.BR send --in / --at ),
the list rendered (
.BR list ),
at least one id was matched (
.BR dismiss ),
the clear completed (
.BR clear ),
the settings printed (
.BR settings ),
or the user interacted with the notification (
.BR send --wait ).
.TP
.B 1
Authorization denied, or a side-effect failed (e.g.
.B --activate-bundle-id
referred to an app that LaunchServices could not find).
.TP
.B 2
.B --wait-timeout
elapsed before the user interacted with the notification.
.TP
.B 3
.B --wait
mode and the user explicitly dismissed the notification (swipe /
"X" / right-click \(-> close).
.TP
.B 4
.B roar dismiss
and NONE of the supplied identifiers matched a delivered or pending
notification.
.TP
.B 64
Invalid arguments (
.BR EX_USAGE ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ROAR_DEBUG
When set to any non-empty value, the click-handler emits verbose
diagnostics to stderr. Off by default to keep credential-bearing URLs
and bundle ids out of the unified log under launchd.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a simple notification:
.PP
.RS
.nf
roar send --body "Build complete"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send a notification that fires in 5 minutes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
roar send --body "Stand-up in 5" --in 5m
.fi
.RE
.PP
Schedule a notification for a specific local time:
.PP
.RS
.nf
roar send --body "Backup window starts now" --at "2026-12-31 03:00"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Block on a yes/no decision:
.PP
.RS
.nf
choice=$(roar send --wait \\
    --body "Deploy to production?" \\
    --action approve:Approve \\
    --action reject:Reject)
case "$choice" in
    approve) deploy ;;
    reject)  echo "cancelled" ;;
    *)       echo "no answer" ;;
esac
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe build output as the body:
.PP
.RS
.nf
make 2>&1 | tail -n 1 | roar send --title "Build" --in 1s
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /System/Library/Sounds
.TQ
.I /Library/Sounds
Directories scanned by the
.B --sound
validator. Files must have a
.B .aiff
or
.B .caf
extension to be picked up by the
.B UserNotifications
framework.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR launchd (8),
.BR osascript (1),
.BR cron (8).
.PP
